1
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:10,040
[Episode 19]

3
00:01:30,230 --> 00:01:31,560
Thank you for coming to see me.

4
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:35,760
I'm not here to interrogate you.

5
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:38,150
I'm here as your friend.

6
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:39,480
I wanted to talk to you.

7
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:42,950
I've already told your colleagues

8
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:44,760
everything I know.

9
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:48,560
Have you ever

10
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:50,120
seen

11
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:51,790
or heard anyone

12
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:54,120
talk about Han Shuang?

13
00:01:58,480 --> 00:01:59,310
Sun Jiahao told me

14
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,350
about your sister's disappearance

15
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:03,640
so I could get close to you.

16
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:06,430
I don't know anything else.

17
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:10,310
Did Sun Jiahao have

18
00:02:10,910 --> 00:02:12,840
any other hideouts or safe houses?

19
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:23,030
How did you usually contact each other?

20
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:26,630
We didn't

21
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:29,030
see each other often.

22
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:31,240
He always called me.

23
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:35,360
When you spoke on the phone,

24
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:38,150
did you hear anything unusual

25
00:02:38,150 --> 00:02:40,520
or anything you may have overlooked?

26
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:44,150
A few times,

27
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:45,520
I could faintly hear

28
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,360
a girl crying on the other end.

29
00:02:47,910 --> 00:02:48,910
Then he'd say

30
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:50,150
that if she didn't obey,

31
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,080
he'd send her to the factory.

32
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:53,000
The factory?

33
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,150
What kind of factory?

34
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,150
I don't know.

35
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:10,750
Han Ning.

36
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:20,240
I'm sorry.

37
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:36,430
We could have been

38
00:03:37,750 --> 00:03:39,120
good friends.

39
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:41,360
Who would have thought...

40
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,150
After you finish serving your sentence,

41
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:52,120
perhaps

42
00:03:53,190 --> 00:03:54,870
we can have a proper drink together.

43
00:04:31,630 --> 00:04:32,720
Where are we?

44
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:38,240
Where is this place?

45
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:39,560
No idea.

46
00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:42,560
How did you get here?

47
00:04:45,070 --> 00:04:46,680
Is anyone there?

48
00:05:18,270 --> 00:05:19,720
Didn't Han Ning wake up?

49
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:20,870
Old He isn't back yet?

50
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:22,040
He's off enjoying himself.

51
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:24,240
Hey.

52
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:27,240
A leader shouldn't gossip
about people behind their backs.

53
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,560
Master.

54
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:31,190
Captain Ren.

55
00:05:31,430 --> 00:05:32,510
How are you feeling?

56
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:33,430
Much better.

57
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,720
I request to return to duty.

58
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:35,360
All right.

59
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:36,560
Since everyone's back,

60
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:37,720
I'd like to say a few words.

61
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:40,070
The Jiang Li murder case
has formally gone to prosecution.

62
00:05:40,430 --> 00:05:40,920
The bureau

63
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:42,430
has nominated us for a commendation.

64
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,920
The truth can be cruel.

65
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,680
But we all know

66
00:05:58,040 --> 00:05:59,680
no matter the reason,

67
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:02,720
we can never seek justice
by fighting evil with evil.

68
00:06:04,430 --> 00:06:06,630
In the Sun Jiahao case,
the chain of evidence is complete.

69
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:07,720
The criminal facts are clear.

70
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,240
Captain Ren.

71
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:09,390
I believe

72
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:11,240
there was a third person
at the crime scene.

73
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:14,750
But I need more evidence
to substantiate that theory.

74
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:16,800
All right.

75
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:20,560
Is everyone there?

76
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:22,240
Uncle He.

77
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:22,630
Hey.

78
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:27,720
I collected a DNA sample
from the fetus in Xiao Ting's body.

79
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:29,040
Guess what I found?

80
00:06:29,950 --> 00:06:30,630
Go on.

81
00:06:31,270 --> 00:06:32,750
I found a match in hospital records:

82
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:34,720
a paternity test from seven years ago.

83
00:06:38,630 --> 00:06:38,920
Take a look.

84
00:06:40,190 --> 00:06:41,510
This man is the baby's father.

85
00:06:56,630 --> 00:06:57,870
Hello.
Who are you looking for?

86
00:06:58,120 --> 00:06:59,800
We're from Criminal Investigation.

87
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,870
We need to ask Mr. Wang Guosheng
a few questions.

88
00:07:03,870 --> 00:07:04,310
Is he home?

89
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:05,510
He's home.

90
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:19,270
That was fast.

91
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,240
Officers,

92
00:07:31,070 --> 00:07:32,600
anything I can do?

93
00:07:34,510 --> 00:07:36,120
Have you been to Night Flight Club?

94
00:07:38,270 --> 00:07:39,270
Night Flight...

95
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:42,600
That rings a bell.

96
00:07:43,190 --> 00:07:46,720
There was definitely demand
for that kind of business back then.

97
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:50,000
I went to quite a few nightclubs

98
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:51,680
and private clubs.

99
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:52,920
Well...

100
00:07:53,510 --> 00:07:55,120
You should know this man, right?

101
00:07:58,240 --> 00:07:59,560
This is a police inquiry.
Be serious.

102
00:08:00,430 --> 00:08:01,240
All right.
I'll be serious.

103
00:08:03,270 --> 00:08:04,390
I stopped going there years ago.

104
00:08:05,190 --> 00:08:06,120
I've turned over a new leaf.

105
00:08:06,430 --> 00:08:07,430
So the prodigal son returned.

106
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:09,750
This woman...

107
00:08:10,510 --> 00:08:11,040
Do you know her?

108
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:19,800
Think carefully before you answer.

109
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:29,720
She doesn't ring a bell.

110
00:08:33,510 --> 00:08:34,320
Let me refresh your memory.

111
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:36,120
Her name is Xiao Ting.

112
00:08:36,910 --> 00:08:38,870
She died seven years ago.

113
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:42,270
Her body was recently found
on Cuiping Mountain.

114
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,720
She was seven months pregnant
when she died.

115
00:08:50,270 --> 00:08:51,000
So?

116
00:08:51,910 --> 00:08:53,030
What does that have to do with me?

117
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:53,870
I don't even know her.

118
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:58,480
Seven years ago, you
had a prenatal paternity test done.

119
00:08:58,790 --> 00:08:59,480
She was carrying

120
00:09:00,150 --> 00:09:01,240
your child.

121
00:09:05,390 --> 00:09:06,510
Now I remember.

122
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,840
That doesn't prove

123
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,630
the baby was mine, does it?

124
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:15,720
She may have been with another man
afterward.

125
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,320
Even after a body has lain dead
for seven years,

126
00:09:17,790 --> 00:09:19,720
we can still collect DNA.

127
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:27,000
Officers,

128
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:27,870
I didn't kill anyone.

129
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:28,910
I swear I didn't kill her.

130
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:32,720
Her pregnancy was completely unexpected.

131
00:09:32,870 --> 00:09:33,510
I gave her money.

132
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:34,630
I gave her a lot of money.

133
00:09:35,270 --> 00:09:36,910
I... I just wanted a child.

134
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:38,270
I could never kill or harm anyone.

135
00:09:38,270 --> 00:09:40,320
You don't even remember
what the mother looked like.

136
00:09:40,390 --> 00:09:41,360
Don't you feel any guilt?

137
00:09:44,910 --> 00:09:46,510
Please come to the station with us.

138
00:09:51,030 --> 00:09:52,000
Back then,

139
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:54,720
I often took my clients

140
00:09:55,550 --> 00:09:56,790
to Night Flight Club.

141
00:09:58,320 --> 00:10:00,670
Over time, I got to know Brother Hao.

142
00:10:00,910 --> 00:10:01,720
Later,

143
00:10:02,670 --> 00:10:04,240
they kept offering me
'new merchandise.'

144
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:06,670
By 'new merchandise,' I mean...

145
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:10,030
That's beside the point.

146
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:10,630
What I mean is...

147
00:10:11,510 --> 00:10:14,720
One day, their manager came to me.

148
00:10:21,270 --> 00:10:21,670
Brother.

149
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:25,960
Brother.

150
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:27,750
Come outside.
I need to talk to you.

151
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:30,670
Brother.

152
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:34,440
Brother.

153
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:35,150
Hey.

154
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:40,360
What is it?

155
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:41,910
Why are you here at this hour?

156
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:43,440
Brother, something happened.

157
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:45,720
That girl from last time is pregnant.

158
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:46,720
It's most likely yours.

159
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:47,670
What do you mean, mine?

160
00:10:48,910 --> 00:10:49,790
Did the police tell you?

161
00:10:49,790 --> 00:10:50,790
Did the doctor tell you?

162
00:10:51,870 --> 00:10:52,200
No.

163
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:54,510
That girl is notoriously stubborn.

164
00:10:54,510 --> 00:10:56,720
Only someone forceful like you
could get your way with her.

165
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:58,720
She was hurt last time
and hasn't been with anyone else.

166
00:10:59,910 --> 00:11:00,910
Mr. Xu.

167
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:02,030
What do you mean?

168
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,910
Brother, I didn't mean anything by it.

169
00:11:05,910 --> 00:11:07,670
I only came to let you know.

170
00:11:07,870 --> 00:11:09,910
Do you want to keep it or abort it?

171
00:11:09,910 --> 00:11:12,120
Either way, I'll need some money.

172
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:14,510
Does

173
00:11:15,390 --> 00:11:16,270
Brother Hao know about this?

174
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:18,440
Huh?

175
00:11:20,510 --> 00:11:21,240
Brother.

176
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:22,750
I shouldn't have said that.

177
00:11:23,390 --> 00:11:23,670
Huh?

178
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:24,510
Fine.

179
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:44,390
Take it.

180
00:11:44,390 --> 00:11:45,910
Wow, Brother.

181
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,120
This is far too generous.

182
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,440
I can't take this much.

183
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:50,960
Tomorrow,

184
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:52,750
find a place

185
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,320
and run a proper test.

186
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,080
If it's mine,

187
00:11:56,630 --> 00:11:57,440
don't worry,

188
00:11:58,240 --> 00:11:59,030
money won't be a problem.

189
00:12:00,270 --> 00:12:01,630
But you have to promise me

190
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,630
you'll keep the baby safe.

191
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:05,240
But if it's not mine,

192
00:12:06,910 --> 00:12:07,630
then Brother Hao

193
00:12:08,910 --> 00:12:10,080
will owe me an explanation.

194
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:11,910
Don't worry, Brother.

195
00:12:11,910 --> 00:12:13,080
That won't be a problem.

196
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:15,080
I'll take care of it for you.

197
00:12:16,630 --> 00:12:17,720
I'm leaving, Brother.

198
00:12:54,330 --> 00:12:56,390
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

199
00:12:56,390 --> 00:12:58,340
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

200
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:00,250
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

201
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:02,060
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

202
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:04,390
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

203
00:13:04,390 --> 00:13:06,820
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

204
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:11,870
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

205
00:13:11,870 --> 00:13:13,760
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

206
00:13:13,770 --> 00:13:15,710
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

207
00:13:15,710 --> 00:13:17,830
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

208
00:13:17,870 --> 00:13:19,840
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

209
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:22,010
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

210
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:29,080
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

211
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:32,450
♪Why is that child crying?♪

212
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:35,150
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

213
00:13:35,150 --> 00:13:36,770
♪Means I've grown up♪

214
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:39,920
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

215
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:43,400
♪The wound still aches♪

216
00:13:43,810 --> 00:13:48,160
♪Like a biting winter♪

217
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:51,430
♪But a spark still glows♪

